docs {
  B2 as a second CEFR level — phase 26.

  WHAT THIS CHECKS
  A B2 seat gets the whole Start experience on Modelltest 7, and a centre
  can run a B2 Exam Day sitting that is timed and marked as B2 rather than
  as B1.

  BEFORE YOU START
  1. Run the API against the disposable database, not production:
         .\scripts\start-dev-testdb.ps1
     It prints the database host. It must NOT be ep-wandering-hall.
  2. Modelltest 7 must be imported on that database:
         npm run modelltest:verify -- --level B2 --number 7
     Expect "Modelltest 7 (B2) verified."
  3. Have a centre signed in (Center Auth / 03 Login) so {{accessToken}}
     is set, and an activation code minted so {{codeId}} is set.

  ORDER
  01 and 02 set the seat to B2 and put a student on it. Everything after
  depends on {{studentAccessToken}} belonging to a B2 student, so run them
  in sequence the first time.

  WHAT WOULD HAVE FAILED BEFORE THIS PHASE
  - 10 Live Room: 400, because the level validator accepted only B1
  - 12 Create B2 sitting: level stamped B1 whatever paper was chosen
  - 13 Hören 20 minutes: timed with B1's 30
  - 07 Schreiben both tasks: only one of the two offered
  - 09 Vocab pack: empty
}
